  "act": 2,
  "description": "Night of September 28-29, 2016. Indian Para SF \u2014 Ghatak platoons of 6 Bihar and 10 Dogra regiments, trained on the terrain \u2014 cross the Line of Control and destroy 7 JeM/LeT infiltration launchpads across 4 sectors in PoK. 35-50 militants killed (Indian estimates; Pakistan denies any strikes occurred). DGMO Lt Gen Ranbir Singh makes a public announcement the next morning \u2014 the first time India officially acknowledged a cross-LOC operation since 1971. Rizwan Shah, whose ground intelligence formed the targeting package, must now manage the aftermath: ISI is conducting a sweep to identify how India knew exact launchpad locations. His cover is at maximum risk in the 72 hours post-strike.",
  "real_world_correlation": {
    "event_date": "September 28-29, 2016",
    "real_event": "Indian Army Para SF conducted simultaneous raids on 7 launchpads across 4 LoC sectors in PoK (Bhimber Gali, Kel, Lipa, Dudhnial). DGMO Lt Gen Ranbir Singh announced at 1615 hours Sept 29 that 'significant casualties' were inflicted. Most Indian media estimates: 35-50 militants killed. Pakistan denied any strikes, claimed only a border skirmish. Pakistan's DGMO called Indian counterpart post-announcement.",
    "units_involved": "Ghatak platoons (elite assault element) of 6 Bihar Regiment and 10 Dogra Regiment. These units were familiar with the terrain \u2014 specifically chosen for the Uri sector. Helicopters used for insertion/extraction.",
    "international_reaction": "US called for de-escalation; China backed Pakistan's narrative of 'border skirmish'. Russia expressed concern. No country other than India acknowledged strikes as surgical cross-LOC operations. Pakistan's denial was strategic \u2014 acknowledging the strikes would have admitted vulnerability of their launchpad infrastructure.",
    "pakistan_denial_logic": "Pakistan's denial served a dual intelligence purpose: (1) avoided admitting ISI-JeM launchpad infrastructure existed as described; (2) prevented domestic political fallout from admitting Indian Army crossed LOC. This denial also meant Pakistan could not officially retaliate without admitting the strikes happened.",
    "doctrine_shift": "The surgical strikes represented India's definitive abandonment of strategic restraint as doctrine. Every post-Uri Indian security response \u2014 Balakot (2019), Operation Sindoor (2025) \u2014 traces its doctrinal permission back to this moment. DGMO's public announcement was deliberate: India chose to go on record, establishing deterrence through demonstrated willingness."
  },
